    # --- WAKING UP SCENE ---
    scene bg byron_bedroom with fade

    "Byron suddenly sits up, waking up abruptly from the dream."

    b "Ugh... my head..."

    "Byron slowly swings his legs off the bed, rubbing his eyes before pulling on his shirt."

    b "Hm... I really miss him. Wish we had contacts with each other..."

    "Byron steps out of his room and walks down the hallway into the kitchen."

    scene bg kitchen with dissolve

    b "Good morning, Ma."

    m "Oh, hey sweetie! Did you get good sleep?"

    b "Yeah... but this dream I had..."

    m "It's about Kishi, isn't it?"

    "Byron's face instantly flushes red at the sudden mention of Kishi's name."

    b "Wh-... how did you know it was him?.."

    m "Oh c'mon sweetie, you tell me every time you have a dream like that. And I know how you interact with him—every time you get flustered when he gets close to you."

    m "Sweetie, I know you're bisexual or whatever you call it. All I care about is if you're happy with it, so am I. Okay?"

    b "Okay Ma, I'm just worried you'll lecture me with those Bible verses and other reasons."

    m "Sweetie, I grew up liking girls too, but when I met your father, I knew I fell in love. What I'm saying is pick the right one for you, whatever your preferences are."

    m "And no, I'm not like those parents who pressure their children with ungodly lectures on how it's a sin. It's a new era today, it's nothing new, so just be yourself and be happy. That's what I never experienced with your grandma, though I know she was very sweet and caring."

    b "I know Ma, I know."

    "Byron steps in and hugs his mother tightly, feeling immensely grateful for how understanding and open she is."

    m "Also sweetie, we're going back to the Philippines soon. You told me you want to go to college there, right? Where Kishi is?"

